<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Prompts Used in Our Pipeline</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure transparency and reproducibility, we provide all prompts used across the four-agent framework. Each agent relies on structured and modular prompts to fulfill its role within the pipeline:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Director Agent Prompts:</span> Used for role setting, symptom screening, and guiding patient agents in both two tasks.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Patient Agent Prompts:</span> Used to simulate patient responses in both medication consultation and disease diagnosis tasks.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Doctor Agent Prompts:</span> Used to elicit diagnoses and treatment suggestions from the evaluated models.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Judge Agent Prompts:</span> Used for multi-dimensional scoring of correctness, completeness, and interaction quality.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Due to space constraints, we display two representative templates in the following pages. The full set of 16 prompt templates is available from the authors upon request.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.12224v1/figures/turn_combine_en.png" id="A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/265;" width="429" height="265" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5. </span>Correctness (a) and History taking scores (b) of eight models in an English disease-diagnosis scenario at different turn counts. Larger circles indicate more cases that ended the dialogue at that turn and received the corresponding score.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.12224v1/figures/director_agent_disease_diagnosis_en.jpeg" id="A1.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/243;" width="429" height="243" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.12224v1/figures/director_agent_medication_consultation_en.jpeg" id="A1.F6.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/252;" width="429" height="252" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6. </span>Prompt templates of the Director Agent for disease diagnosis and medication consultation in English.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Model Descriptions</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix B Model Descriptions ‣ MedKGEval: A Knowledge Graph-Based Multi-Turn Evaluation Framework for Open-Ended Patient Interactions with Clinical LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> provides a brief overview of the eight evaluated models, including model size, training type (general vs. medical-specific), and open-source status. This serves to contextualize performance differences observed in Section <span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Experiments</span>.</p>
</div>
